1
00:00:06,923 --> 00:00:11,423
-And now the Kung Pao Chicken.
-Yeah, smooth. Ha, ha.

2
00:00:11,677 --> 00:00:15,263
And finally, my Moo Shu Pork.

3
00:00:17,767 --> 00:00:19,685
LEONARD:
Whoo-hoo!

4
00:00:19,852 --> 00:00:24,273
There you have it, gentlemen.
Our entire dinner unpacked by robot.

5
00:00:24,440 --> 00:00:26,442
And it only took 28 minutes.

6
00:00:27,777 --> 00:00:31,113
-Impressive, but we must be cautious.
-Why?

7
00:00:31,614 --> 00:00:34,366
Today,
it's a Chinese-food-retrieval robot.

8
00:00:34,534 --> 00:00:39,034
Tomorrow, it travels back in time
and tries to kill Sarah Connor.

9
00:00:39,789 --> 00:00:41,457
I don't think that's gonna happen,
Sheldon.

10
00:00:41,624 --> 00:00:44,376
No one ever does.
That's why it happens.

11
00:00:46,087 --> 00:00:47,379
Hey. Is the food here?

12
00:00:47,880 --> 00:00:48,922
Ooh, what's that?

13
00:00:49,090 --> 00:00:52,343
That, dear lady,
is the Wolowitz Programmable Hand...

14
00:00:52,510 --> 00:00:56,514
...designed for extravehicular repairs
on the International Space Station.

15
00:00:56,681 --> 00:00:59,850
-Oh, cool.
-Ask me to pass the soy sauce.

16
00:01:00,017 --> 00:01:02,602
Oh, does that come up much
on the Space Station?

17
00:01:03,062 --> 00:01:05,981
Mostly with Asian
and Jewish astronauts.

18
00:01:06,524 --> 00:01:09,276
-All right, pass the soy sauce.
-Coming up.

19
00:01:09,443 --> 00:01:10,986
[CLEARS THROAT]

20
00:01:11,946 --> 00:01:13,739
[KEYBOARD CLICKING]

21
00:01:15,908 --> 00:01:18,160
[KEYBOARD CONTINUES CLICKING]

22
00:01:20,246 --> 00:01:23,249
-So how's work?
-Oh, It's not bad.

23
00:01:23,416 --> 00:01:26,252
-Kind of hungry.
-Yeah, we all are.

24
00:01:26,419 --> 00:01:28,129
Just wait.

25
00:01:28,337 --> 00:01:31,214
You realize, Penny, that the technology
that went into this arm...

26
00:01:31,382 --> 00:01:35,344
...will one day make unskilled
food servers such as yourself obsolete.

27
00:01:36,137 --> 00:01:39,223
Really? They're gonna make a robot
that spits on your hamburger?

28
00:01:41,726 --> 00:01:44,145
I thought you broke up with her.
Why is she here?

29
00:01:45,396 --> 00:01:49,024
Okay, here we go.
Passing the soy sauce.

30
00:01:50,651 --> 00:01:52,527
Put out your hand.

31
00:01:56,240 --> 00:01:58,158
[PENNY CHUCKLES]

32
00:01:58,326 --> 00:02:00,661
-That's amazing.
-I wouldn't say "amazing."

33
00:02:00,870 --> 00:02:02,705
At best, it's a modest leap forward...

34
00:02:02,872 --> 00:02:06,917
...from the basic technology
that gave us Country Bear Jamboree.

35
00:02:08,544 --> 00:02:10,379
-Hey, Sheldon? Ahem.
-Yes?

36
00:02:18,638 --> 00:02:22,391
-Peace?
-No, not peace. Hang on.

37
00:02:49,752 --> 00:02:52,713
Does NASA know you're using that thing
as a napkin holder?

38
00:02:52,880 --> 00:02:56,300
Are you kidding? They still think
it's in a secure locker at JPL.

39
00:02:57,593 --> 00:02:59,761
-You stole it?
-Borrowed.

40
00:02:59,929 --> 00:03:03,641
The trick is to carry it out to your car
like you own it.

41
00:03:03,808 --> 00:03:04,934
[CELL PHONE BEEPS]

42
00:03:05,101 --> 00:03:06,519
Excuse me.

43
00:03:08,312 --> 00:03:12,812
Oh, Amy's at the dry-cleaner's
and she's made a very amusing pun.

44
00:03:13,526 --> 00:03:18,026
Ahem. "I don't care for perchloroethylene
and I don't like glycol ether."

45
00:03:24,578 --> 00:03:28,623
Get it? She doesn't like glycol ether.

46
00:03:30,793 --> 00:03:32,336
Sounds like "either."

47
00:03:33,921 --> 00:03:35,255
[GIGGLES]

48
00:03:37,299 --> 00:03:39,426
"L_O_L."

49
00:03:39,844 --> 00:03:40,928
Who's Amy?

50
00:03:41,095 --> 00:03:43,138
-His girlfriend.
-Sheldon has a girlfriend?

51
00:03:43,305 --> 00:03:45,265
-She's not my girlfriend.
-How long?

52
00:03:45,433 --> 00:03:47,309
-Four months.
-She's not my girlfriend.

53
00:03:47,476 --> 00:03:49,978
For four months
I have been asking you what's new.

54
00:03:50,146 --> 00:03:52,982
You never thought to go with
"Sheldon has a girlfriend"?

55
00:03:53,149 --> 00:03:55,317
-She's not my girlfriend.
-Teh, teh, teh.

56
00:03:55,484 --> 00:03:58,361
-How did they meet?
-Raj and I entered Sheldon's information...

57
00:03:58,571 --> 00:04:01,782
...on a dating site
and it spit out Amy Farrah Fowler.

58
00:04:01,949 --> 00:04:04,117
Oh, my God! Sheldon and Amy.

59
00:04:04,285 --> 00:04:05,828
Or as we call them, "Shamy."

60
00:04:05,995 --> 00:04:07,162
[PENNY SQUEALS]

61
00:04:07,830 --> 00:04:10,290
Shamy. I am so digging the Shamy.

62
00:04:10,458 --> 00:04:13,002
All right. Everyone, pay attention.

63
00:04:13,169 --> 00:04:16,005
Yes, I have a friend named
Amy Farrah Fowler.

64
00:04:16,172 --> 00:04:17,339
Yes, she is female.

65
00:04:17,506 --> 00:04:22,006
Yes, we communicate on a daily basis,
but no, she is not my girlfriend.

66
00:04:22,803 --> 00:04:25,055
Okay, well,
what do you communicate about?

67
00:04:25,222 --> 00:04:28,516
Well, my work in physics,
her work in neurobiology...

68
00:04:28,684 --> 00:04:31,895
...and most recently, the possibility
of our having a child together.

69
00:04:40,321 --> 00:04:41,697
Thank you.

70
00:04:43,199 --> 00:04:45,534
Wait a minute, a child?
You never see this girl.

71
00:04:45,701 --> 00:04:47,744
You just e-mail and text and Twitter...

72
00:04:47,912 --> 00:04:50,372
...and now you're considering
having a baby?

73
00:04:50,539 --> 00:04:52,707
Amy pointed out
that between the two of us...

74
00:04:52,875 --> 00:04:56,044
...our genetic material
has the potential of producing the first...

75
00:04:56,212 --> 00:04:59,089
...In a line of intellectually superior
benign overlords...

76
00:04:59,256 --> 00:05:02,384
...to guide humanity
to a brighter tomorrow.

77
00:05:04,553 --> 00:05:07,097
I'm guessing that future historians
will condemn us...

78
00:05:07,264 --> 00:05:10,767
...for not taking this opportunity
to kill Sheldon.

79
00:05:11,560 --> 00:05:14,437
-Okay. I have a question.
-Yes, Penny.

80
00:05:14,647 --> 00:05:17,858
You don't even like people touching you.
How are you gonna have sex?

81
00:05:19,902 --> 00:05:21,570
Why on earth would we have sex?

82
00:05:23,948 --> 00:05:26,533
Oh, honey, did your mom
not have the talk with you?

83
00:05:26,700 --> 00:05:30,120
You know, when your private parts
started growing?

84
00:05:30,287 --> 00:05:33,248
I'm quite aware of the way
humans usually reproduce...

85
00:05:33,415 --> 00:05:35,041
...which is messy, unsanitary...

86
00:05:35,209 --> 00:05:37,711
...and based on living next to you
for three years...

87
00:05:37,878 --> 00:05:41,590
...Involves loud and unnecessary appeals
to a deity.

88
00:05:41,757 --> 00:05:44,176
-Oh, God.
-Yes, exactly.

89
00:05:47,429 --> 00:05:51,224
Consequently, if Amy and I choose
to bring new life into this world...

90
00:05:51,392 --> 00:05:53,310
...It will be accomplished clinically...

91
00:05:53,477 --> 00:05:56,313
...with fertility experts in a lab
with Petri dishes.

92
00:05:56,480 --> 00:06:00,275
Which reminds me, you have broad hips
and a certain corn-fed vigor.

93
00:06:00,442 --> 00:06:03,111
Is your womb available for rental?

94
00:06:05,322 --> 00:06:07,615
Still digging the Shamy?

95
00:06:08,742 --> 00:06:11,870
Look, Sheldon, before you race off
to the fertility clinic...

96
00:06:12,037 --> 00:06:13,371
...you might wanna think about...

97
00:06:13,539 --> 00:06:16,792
...gee, I don't know, maybe actually
spending some time with her.

98
00:06:16,959 --> 00:06:18,794
-You mean dating?
-Yeah.

99
00:06:18,961 --> 00:06:20,462
-I can't date Amy.
-Why not?

100
00:06:20,629 --> 00:06:22,297
She's not my girlfriend.

101
00:06:22,464 --> 00:06:24,466
Don't think of it as dating a girlfriend.

102
00:06:24,633 --> 00:06:28,219
Think of it as, uh, getting to know
the future mother of your child.

103
00:06:28,429 --> 00:06:30,347
Oh.

104
00:06:30,514 --> 00:06:32,474
I hadn't considered that.

105
00:06:32,641 --> 00:06:35,310
I suppose she will have to have
access to our progeny.

106
00:06:35,477 --> 00:06:39,814
And you don't think I can achieve
the required intimacy via text messaging?

107
00:06:40,316 --> 00:06:42,026
-Probably not.
-Hmm.

108
00:06:42,818 --> 00:06:46,988
It would appear as if the phone
companies have been lying to me.

109
00:06:49,491 --> 00:06:53,286
Penny. Penny. Penny.

110
00:06:54,788 --> 00:06:57,373
You do realize
I stand on the other side of the door...

111
00:06:57,541 --> 00:07:00,126
...waiting for you
to finish knocking three times.

112
00:07:00,294 --> 00:07:03,380
I know. I can see the shadow
of your feet under the door.

113
00:07:04,173 --> 00:07:06,341
Yeah. My point is it's a waste of time.

114
00:07:06,508 --> 00:07:09,052
If you're looking for an example
of a waste of time. ..

115
00:07:09,261 --> 00:07:12,180
...I would refer you to the conversation
we're having right now.

116
00:07:12,348 --> 00:07:14,975
-What do you want?
-I've decided to take your advice...

117
00:07:15,142 --> 00:07:17,686
...and have arranged to go on a date
with Amy Farrah Fowler.

118
00:07:17,853 --> 00:07:21,523
-Oh, that's great. Have fun.
“Wait. You have to drive me.

119
00:07:21,690 --> 00:07:23,983
-What?
-You know I don't drive.

120
00:07:24,151 --> 00:07:25,485
-Well, go ask Leonard.
- I did.

121
00:07:25,653 --> 00:07:30,153
He said, and I quote, "Ask Penny.
It was her cockamamie idea."

122
00:07:31,283 --> 00:07:32,575
Leonard said "cockamamie"?

123
00:07:32,785 --> 00:07:36,371
Actually, I'm paraphrasing. Having
been raised in a Christian household. ..

124
00:07:36,538 --> 00:07:39,415
...I'm uncomfortable
with the language he used.

125
00:07:39,917 --> 00:07:43,045
And to be honest, I'm not
entirely comfortable with "cockamamie.”

126
00:07:43,879 --> 00:07:45,213
Okay, fine. When's the date?

127
00:07:45,381 --> 00:07:46,840
-Now.
-Now?

128
00:07:47,007 --> 00:07:48,717
Hurry, we're going to be late.

129
00:07:50,344 --> 00:07:53,555
Sheldon, did it ever occur to you
that I might have other plans?

130
00:07:53,722 --> 00:07:57,016
I'm sorry. Do you have other plans?

131
00:07:59,812 --> 00:08:02,231
Well, no, not per se, but....

132
00:08:02,856 --> 00:08:07,356
And so this conversation is as pointless
as your door-knocking soliloquy?

133
00:08:09,071 --> 00:08:12,324
Let me get my cockamamie keys.

134
00:08:14,868 --> 00:08:18,079
HOWARD:
Oh, God, that feels so good.

135
00:08:18,330 --> 00:08:20,081
[I MOANING]

136
00:08:22,751 --> 00:08:25,962
Yeah, that's the spot. Oh, baby.

137
00:08:26,130 --> 00:08:29,258
MRS. WOLOWITZ:
Howard, dinner's ready!

138
00:08:29,425 --> 00:08:32,553
I'll eat later, I'm busy!

139
00:08:33,053 --> 00:08:36,431
Oh, yeah. Just like a real hand.

140
00:08:43,814 --> 00:08:45,398
Hmm.

141
00:08:49,236 --> 00:08:52,781
-Thank you for driving me.
You're welcome.

142
00:08:53,782 --> 00:08:58,282
I wish you weren't wearing flip-flops.
Dangerous to drive in flip-flops.

143
00:08:58,662 --> 00:09:00,664
-Sheldon.
-Sorry.

144
00:09:00,873 --> 00:09:04,459
I just don't wanna be
yet another flip-flop fatality.

145
00:09:06,795 --> 00:09:08,463
Can I ask you a question?

146
00:09:08,630 --> 00:09:10,632
Given your
community-college education...

147
00:09:10,799 --> 00:09:13,635
...I encourage you to ask me
as many as possible.

148
00:09:15,137 --> 00:09:19,599
Yeah, ahem, well, my question is,
and I'm pretty sure I know the answer...

149
00:09:19,767 --> 00:09:21,393
...is this your first date?

150
00:09:21,977 --> 00:09:23,603
That depends.

151
00:09:23,771 --> 00:09:25,647
Does square dancing with my sister...

152
00:09:25,814 --> 00:09:29,526
...at a Teens for Jesus
Fourth of July hoedown count as a date?

153
00:09:30,486 --> 00:09:33,197
-No.
-Then this is my first date.

154
00:09:34,406 --> 00:09:37,409
Okay, well, then there's a couple of things
you should probably know.

155
00:09:38,160 --> 00:09:40,996
I have a master's degree
and two doctorates.

156
00:09:41,163 --> 00:09:44,666
The things I should know, I do know.

157
00:09:45,459 --> 00:09:48,503
My point is,
I know more about dating than you...

158
00:09:48,670 --> 00:09:52,340
...and if you were as smart as you think
you are, you would listen to me.

159
00:09:52,549 --> 00:09:55,510
If you know so much,
how come I have a date tonight...

160
00:09:55,677 --> 00:09:59,180
...and you have nothing better to do
than drive me to it?

161
00:10:01,725 --> 00:10:03,643
Fair point.

162
00:10:06,063 --> 00:10:09,066
You know, there's something I've
always wondered about Aquaman.

163
00:10:09,566 --> 00:10:12,193
-Yeah?
-Where does he poop?

164
00:10:14,696 --> 00:10:18,157
-What?
“What would a toilet look like in Atlantis?

165
00:10:18,325 --> 00:10:21,161
How would you flush it?
And when you did flush it...

166
00:10:21,328 --> 00:10:23,204
...where would the poop go?

167
00:10:25,290 --> 00:10:26,708
[PHONE RINGS]

168
00:10:26,875 --> 00:10:28,543
Hold that thought.

169
00:10:29,545 --> 00:10:31,672
Hey, Howard, what's going on?

170
00:10:32,089 --> 00:10:35,717
Wha--? Hold on. Howard.
Howard, slow down.

171
00:10:35,884 --> 00:10:38,386
The robot hand
is stuck on your what?

172
00:10:42,099 --> 00:10:44,476
You're not gonna believe this.

173
00:10:58,448 --> 00:10:59,574
[PENNY CLEARS THROAT]

174
00:10:59,741 --> 00:11:04,241
So, um, Amy, Sheldon tells me
you're a neuro-something-or-other.

175
00:11:05,581 --> 00:11:07,916
Neurobiologist.

176
00:11:08,083 --> 00:11:10,668
Your "check engine” light is on.

177
00:11:12,296 --> 00:11:13,505
Yeah, it's okay.

178
00:11:13,672 --> 00:11:15,840
-But the light indicates--
-Don't bother.

179
00:11:16,008 --> 00:11:20,508
I've wasted many an hour
tilting at that particular windmill.

180
00:11:22,806 --> 00:11:25,391
What is that scent you're wearing?
It smells great.

181
00:11:25,934 --> 00:11:27,602
Dandruff shampoo.

182
00:11:29,396 --> 00:11:31,606
I have dry scalp.

183
00:11:31,773 --> 00:11:34,942
Ah, well, your hair looks very nice.

184
00:11:35,611 --> 00:11:37,988
Are you a homosexual?

185
00:11:38,947 --> 00:11:43,447
-No, I was just giving you a compliment.
-Hmm.

186
00:11:43,619 --> 00:11:46,538
I would have been more flattered
if you were a homosexual.

187
00:11:49,333 --> 00:11:52,461
-Guys, how about some music?
-Oh, I wouldn't care for that.

188
00:11:52,628 --> 00:11:54,296
-Amy?
-No, thank you.

189
00:11:55,130 --> 00:11:58,967
Okay. Uncomfortable silence it is.

190
00:12:03,055 --> 00:12:04,973
Hey, Sheldon, have you told Amy...

191
00:12:05,140 --> 00:12:07,517
...what it was like for you
growing up in Texas?

192
00:12:07,684 --> 00:12:09,227
No.

193
00:12:10,812 --> 00:12:12,980
Well, why don't you tell her?

194
00:12:13,857 --> 00:12:15,483
All right.

195
00:12:15,734 --> 00:12:17,444
It was hell.

196
00:12:19,446 --> 00:12:20,655
Any follow-up, Amy?

197
00:12:22,366 --> 00:12:23,575
No.

198
00:12:28,497 --> 00:12:32,167
I, myself, grew up in Nebraska.
Small town outside of Omaha.

199
00:12:32,334 --> 00:12:36,834
Yeah, nice place, mostly family farms,
a few meth labs.

200
00:12:37,673 --> 00:12:40,842
I'm sorry, how is this better
than uncomfortable silence?

201
00:12:41,009 --> 00:12:43,344
I don't know.
I was just trying something.

202
00:12:45,389 --> 00:12:47,265
Muggles.

203
00:12:53,689 --> 00:12:57,067
You slipped and fell into a robot hand?

204
00:12:59,569 --> 00:13:00,861
Yes.

205
00:13:01,989 --> 00:13:03,532
Penis first.

206
00:13:07,077 --> 00:13:08,870
Yes. Now, help me!

207
00:13:09,037 --> 00:13:10,288
I'd suggest a lubricant...

208
00:13:10,497 --> 00:13:13,875
...but I have a feeling
you fell on some of that as well.

209
00:13:14,042 --> 00:13:15,293
Not funny, Leonard.

210
00:13:15,502 --> 00:13:18,296
Really? A robot hand's
got a death grip on your junk, dude.

211
00:13:18,463 --> 00:13:19,505
That's funny, ask anyone.

212
00:13:19,673 --> 00:13:20,715
[BOTH LAUGH]

213
00:13:21,216 --> 00:13:23,885
Please, before my mother walks in,
get this off me.

214
00:13:24,052 --> 00:13:25,094
Okay, let's see.

215
00:13:25,262 --> 00:13:26,888
No. Don't touch.
The program is paused.

216
00:13:27,055 --> 00:13:29,557
-Then let's unpause it.
- I loaded the wrong program.

217
00:13:29,725 --> 00:13:31,768
The hand thinks
it's holding a screwdriver.

218
00:13:31,935 --> 00:13:34,896
If you continue the program,
it's gonna start twisting.

219
00:13:36,732 --> 00:13:39,234
All-- All-- All right, how about this?

220
00:13:39,401 --> 00:13:43,405
When Winnie the Pooh
got his head stuck in the honey tree...

221
00:13:43,572 --> 00:13:47,242
...his friends all grabbed onto him
and pulled and pulled.

222
00:13:49,536 --> 00:13:52,997
You do what you want. I'm not touching
another man's honey tree.

223
00:13:53,665 --> 00:13:55,249
All right, uh, forget pulling.

224
00:13:55,417 --> 00:13:57,836
How about we get an electric saw
and cut it off?

225
00:13:58,045 --> 00:13:59,629
What? No saws!

226
00:13:59,796 --> 00:14:02,757
One circumcision was enough.

227
00:14:05,260 --> 00:14:06,970
How about an acetylene torch?

228
00:14:07,179 --> 00:14:09,431
I can't believe
this needs to be said out loud.

229
00:14:09,598 --> 00:14:13,435
-No pulling, no saws, no torches.
-Then what do you want us to do?

230
00:14:13,602 --> 00:14:15,729
MRS. WOLOWITZ:
Howard, I made cookies for you...

231
00:14:15,896 --> 00:14:18,148
...and your little friends!

232
00:14:18,607 --> 00:14:20,358
That's great, Mom, thanks!

233
00:14:20,567 --> 00:14:23,278
MRS. WOLOWITZ:
I'll bring them up with Hawaiian Punch!

234
00:14:23,445 --> 00:14:25,447
-Don't come up here!
MRS WOLOWITZ: Why not?

235
00:14:25,614 --> 00:14:27,616
Are you ashamed of your mother?

236
00:14:27,783 --> 00:14:30,368
Yes, but that's not the point!

237
00:14:31,370 --> 00:14:32,454
Get me out of here.

